Problem Statement:
Given an array of integers nums, find all the leaders in the array.

An element is called a leader if it is strictly greater than all the elements to its right.
- The rightmost element is always a leader because there are no elements to its right.
- If an element is equal to or smaller than any element to its right, it is not a leader.
- Return all leaders in the same order as they appear in the original array.

Example:
Input:
nums = [16, 17, 4, 3, 5, 2]
Output:
[17, 5, 2]

Brute Force Approach
Concept: Check every element against all the elements present on its right side.
For every element at index i:
1. Assume the current element is a leader.
2. Traverse all elements from i+1 to n-1.
3. If any element is greater than or equal to the current element, it is not a leader.
4. If no such element exists, add it to the answer.
5. Repeat for every element.

Code:
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> leaders(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<int> ans;
        int n = nums.size();

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            bool isLeader = true;

            for(int j = i+1; j < n; j++) {
                if(nums[j] >= nums[i]) {
                    isLeader = false;
                    break;
                }
            }

            if(isLeader) {
                ans.push_back(nums[i]);
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
Time Complexity: O(n²)
Space Complexity: O(1)
Output Space: O(n)


Optimal Approach:Traversing from Right to Left
Concept: Instead of repeatedly checking all elements to the right, maintain the maximum element encountered so far.
Since we are traversing from right to left, the maximum value (maxi) represents the greatest element among all elements to the right of the current element.

Algorithm / Steps:
1. Create an empty vector ans to store leaders.
2. Initialize maxi = INT_MIN.
3. Start traversing the array from the last index (n-1) towards index 0.
4. Compare the current element with maxi.
5. If nums[i] > maxi:
   - The current element is a leader.
   - Add it to the answer vector.
   - Update maxi = nums[i].
6. If the condition is false, skip the element.
7. Reverse the answer vector to maintain the original array order.
8. Return the answer vector.

Code:
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> leaders(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<int> ans;
        int maxi = INT_MIN;

        for(int i = nums.size()-1; i >= 0; i--) {

            if(nums[i] > maxi) {
                ans.push_back(nums[i]);
                maxi = nums[i];
            }
        }

        reverse(ans.begin(), ans.end());

        return ans;
    }
};
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
Output Space Complexity: O(n)
